  "raw_text": "Yes. `git reset --hard` discards uncommitted changes to tracked files in both the working tree and staging area, resetting them to the chosen commit (default: `HEAD`).\n\nIt does **not normally delete untracked files**, though related commands such as `git clean` can.\n\nBefore using it, consider saving changes with:\n\n```bash\ngit stash -u\n```\n\nRecovery may be difficult or impossible if the changes were never committed or stashed.",
